{
  "_about": "cc-P180 / cc-P181: the look rules for build_burrows.py. One seed per zone (change it for a new layout, keep it for the same one); tile weights are relative (any scale); every id is a stock EA tile id as a hex string. Walls: ew = the piece whose slab sits on its tile's SOUTH edge (runs along x), ns = slab on the EAST edge (runs along y), corner = both slabs, post = the SE corner point only; see notes/uo-wall-orientation.md. frameNS / frameEW: how a gap through a north-south / east-west wall is framed (first = the first open tile, mid = the other open tiles, after / before = the wall tiles past and before the gap; replaces false keeps the run piece beside the jamb, as the dungeon set does on OSI's map). Decor rules: where = nearWall | open | any | wallFace (floor tiles just south or east of a wall tile); density = clusters per eligible tile; cluster = [min, max] pieces; radius = cluster spread (Chebyshev); spacing = least distance between cluster centres; z = offsets drawn at random. corners: per zone, what every inner corner gets (item zones: floor = passable pieces on the corner floor tile, torch = a wall torch on the north or west wall, strip = pieces on the visible wall tiles south and east of the corner, pillar = a column on the SE corner tile of rooms at least minRoom on both sides; cave zones: ring = a cluster on the rock ring round the corner, convex = one piece on the rock tip the floor wraps round). gapFrame: the pieces on the rock either end of a cave gap. ringEdge: the cave ring's floor-level tile is a cave edge tile (cave floor with a black wedge toward the rock, Khaldun's pattern) instead of rock; tried on the Tangle in P181 and turned off (on our one-tile sloped ring the wedge stretches into black teeth; Khaldun keeps that tile flat), kept as an option for a build with a two-tile foot. Impassable pieces are kept off narrow paths and spawner homes by the builder; corner pieces on floor tiles are always passable.",
